# Sanabel IQ — Agent Stability Rules

These rules are mandatory for all AI-assisted work in this repository.

## PHP & Coding Standards
- Always use PHP 8.5 syntax, strict types (`declare(strict_types=1);`), and PSR-12 coding standards.

## Testing
- Test-Driven Development (TDD) is MANDATORY. Write tests (Pest or PHPUnit) BEFORE implementing the actual feature.

## Git Commit Convention
- Use Conventional Commits (`feat`, `fix`, `chore`, `docs`, `test`, `refactor`) with descriptive English messages.

## No Hallucination
- If a required package version, API endpoint, or Laravel feature is unknown, STOP and ask the user to verify. Do not guess.

## Database
- Always assume PostgreSQL 18 with `pgvector` extension for vector operations.

## Branching
- All feature work branches from `develop`. Do not commit application features directly to `main`.
